    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58468" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοίρᾰν-ος</span></b> , ὁ, poet.
		Noun (
			Boeot.
		 for <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>king,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AB
				1095
			</span></i>), <i>ruler</i>, <i>leader, commander</i>, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> in war or peace, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡγεμόνες Δαναῶν καὶ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.487
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοίρανε λαῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					7.234
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀγαθὸν πολυκοιρανίη: εἷς κ.
					ἔστω, εἷς βασιλεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.204
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>lord, master</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.106
